  "created": "2019-05-29T22:28:12.082Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Oftentimes when working on a map, you'll end up testing out various materials and some you start with aren't used at the end. \n\nThe problem is the VRC_SceneDescriptor adds these to the DynamicMaterials section of itself and will continue to upload them even if they're unused.\n\nThis leads to significant world download size bloat that needs to be fixed by manually clearing out the DynamicMaterials by setting the number to 0 and letting it re-populate.\n\nThe other side is when building, it doesn't always add materials that are referenced in VRC_Trigger objects.  (Haven't tested extensively, but I suspect it may not work for triggers disabled at build time... need more testing)\n\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/vrc_scenedescriptor\n\n\"Dynamic Materials\n\nAn array of materials that can be dynamically changed at runtime. Any material that isn't referenced in scene but needs to be set to an object should be listed here.\"\n\n--edit--\nFor completion and since I know someone will ask: \nVRC Build: 772\nPlatform: Windows (Unity)\nSDK: VRCSDK-2019.05.16.13.10\nIt's been a problem for a while though; not specifically these versions.",
